WEBVTT

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.510
Welcome back.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.010
I'm home.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:49.250
O Master Kumai, the miko of Kumade Village has come bearing offerings.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:57.340
Please bestow upon me the divine revelation of the mountain gods.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.180
Looks delicious!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:21.400
What's this? You want to go to school in the city?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.820
That's two hours from here.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.530
Way too far.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.740
And now, we're done.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:33.580
Mind if I take this off?
My shoulders are killing me.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.620
I'm going.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.460
No matter what.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.070
Absolutely not!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.210
Listen, Machi.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:18.330
Life in a big city can be tough.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:25.590
If you're not ready, it'll eat you alive.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.930
Sure, there's a lot going on there.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.600
Dreams, fateful encounters...

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.560
And yes, those are the spice of life.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.810
But there are those who can handle the big city

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.730
and those who can't.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.990
You, Machi...

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.570
undoubtedly fall into the latter!

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.080
Why?!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:55.540
You've lived up in the mountains long
enough to develop a bumpkin complex.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.710
You're almost too shy to go
shopping in the next town over.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.250
Plus you're the ultimate klutz with machines.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.800
You still boil rice on the sto—

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.340
Shut up, shut up!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.840
I can't take it anymore!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.720
I can't stand this boring, dwindling village.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.060
There's no signal.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.390
No trains.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:20.350
No people. Just monkeys.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.900
No shops that are ever open.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.820
The convenience store isn't 24/7.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.610
The people are all distant.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.070
Nothing happens.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:32.280
Nobody wants to develop the town.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.450
I'm sick of this village!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.420
This crappy, boring village...

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.540
No asphalt. No street signs.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.920
Okay, I get it.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.460
Don't call it "crappy."

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.970
I don't want to stay here.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.970
I want to leave and go see the world.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:57.730
I don't want to be an ignorant child anymore!

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.480
You've grown up, Machi.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.490
I knew this day would come.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.110
You used to cry about everything at school.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:19.540
I knew I couldn't always be there to console you.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.330
You've grown strong.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.250
You can make your own decisions now.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.010
But...

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:32.760
It still hurts.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:36.640
Natsu...

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:42.480
You won't play with me anymore! I'll miss you!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.860
We grew up together, didn't we?

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:46.860
Natsu.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.150
Natsu.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.360
Machi...

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.490
Mr. Bear!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.120
Mr. Bear, where are you?

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.990
I fell down.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.370
That tickles!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.630
Mr. Bear!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.170
Natsu...

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:08.340
Natsu!

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.460
Hey.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.470
Hurry up the flashback, Natsu.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:25.730
Well, before you make a hasty decision...

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.690
The City Girl Quiz!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.950
Wh-What?

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:43.870
I shall now quiz you on must-know facts for living in the city.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.580
If you get the answers wrong...

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.340
...be a good girl and go to school here.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.760
What happened to making my own decisions?

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.880
Don't worry. It's super easy.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.970
Just fun little questions.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.760
That's not the issue!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.350
Machi, are you afraid you'll fail?

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.520
I look forward to watching you cry later.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:13.400
Let's save that for your wedding day, shall we?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.400
Question 1!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.410
What can you use to go through the ticket gates at the train station?

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.120
Choice 1: Suica (Watermelon).

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.330
Choice 2: Apple.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.700
Choice 3: Banana.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.960
I-I have no idea.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.420
A ticket.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.300
Please choose one of the three.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:40.720
What's this about? Have riders reverted to the barter system?

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.180
I don't know what fruits city people like!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.730
Don't leave me in suspense, Machi.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.770
Y-You're cheating, Natsu!

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:53.110
Doesn't it depend on the station employees' tastes?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.110
Wait, what?

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.280
What did you say?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.660
N-Nothing!

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.410
Uh-oh! Apparently I said something off base.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.500
What now? I don't know the answer!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.250
Maybe it's bananas, since they're sold year-round...

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.670
"Suika" means watermelon, but he spelled it wrong—gotta be a trap.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:18.300
No, wait, one of those things
is definitely not like the others.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:22.300
Two are fruits, but watermelon is actually a vegetable!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.310
Which means...

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.980
The employees like vegetables!

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.600
The answer is number 1!

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:30.100
You're right.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.020
Yay!

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.030
Machi, do you know what "Suica" means?

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:41.820
Come on, everyone does.
By the way, you're saying it funny.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.950
On to question 2, then.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.710
How do you read this sign?

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:55.710
O—

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.260
It is not "oi oi."

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.140
You have twenty seconds.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:04.600
20, 19,18...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.600
Wait! They're not English letters?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.980
17,16,15...

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:10.140
14, 13...

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.140
What is this?

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.730
12,11,10...

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.060
Wait, wait!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:18.860
Nimph, mrmph, 7, 6, 5...

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.030
Stop the countdown!

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.740
I don't know this!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:22.820
4, 3, 2, 1.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:23.950
Time's up!

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.870
No fair...

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:35.540
I thought I'd finally get out of the village, but I'm trapped here forever...

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.460
My whole life!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:40.470
The correct answer was "Marui."

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.010
What the heck?!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.090
Where do you get that from?

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.890
Machi, calm down.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.270
How could <i>any</i>one know that?!

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.140
Who's idea was that?

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.100
Only a true hick would get this angry about it.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:56.940
Don't call me a hick!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.040
Residents of Kumade Village!

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.750
Bears have been sighted in the area.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.960
Please remain in your homes.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:20.800
There's no-one out here.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.220
Still gotta do our jobs.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.390
It's true!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.060
Really?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.520
Let's test it at school sometime.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.680
Hey, you kids!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.100
A cop car!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.020
It's a patrol car.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:38.320
There are bears out today, so go on home!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.030
Yoshio told us to meet him here.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.360
"Yoshio"?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:46.910
Here I am! Sorry!

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.540
There's bears wandering around here, sir. Take the kids inside.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.790
Sure, right away!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:56.830
Who are you? What are you doing in the woods with these kids?

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:02.590
Let me introduce myself! I'm the Kumade
Village Health Department's "Zest Officer,"

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:04.220
Amayadori Yoshio!

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.800
Uh-huh... And what's a village officer doing with these kids?

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.680
Sir, I'm doing the annual telling of our village's lore!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.180
He's getting questioned.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.680
Questioned!

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.020
Excuse me, may I photograph your car?

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:19.440
I love patrol cars! Too cool!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.440
I really wish I'd applied for the police!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.440
Okay, whatever. Just get indoors quick!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:27.950
I wanted to, but Grammy stopped me.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:32.830
Sheesh. These Kumade villagers never take the threat seriously.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:38.170
Well, living so far up the mountain, the bears are probably old friends.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.460
That might be true.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.600
Once upon a time...

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.600
...there was a giant, man-eating bear on Mt. Kumade.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.600
The villagers—

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.640
Don't tell it in that dumb voice.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.310
Quit doing impressions. They don't suit you.

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:03.190
The villagers were at the end of their rope.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.110
I want juice.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.110
Who still tells stories with picture cards?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.940
Because the god of the mountain...

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.940
Use PowerPoint!

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.780
...took the form of a bear,

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.780
How long will this take?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.580
...the people saw all bears as gods.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:21.750
And so, with no recourse, each year
they sacrificed a village maiden to it.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.250
I can barely understand him...

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.260
I've never suffered like this before.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.260
Come on! What a bad student.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.720
I heard this story lots in nursery school!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.600
The mountain god came and
got the bear to mend his ways,

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.350
and then he lived in harmony with the villagers, right?

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.270
Happily ever after, the end!

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.690
Don't reduce it to one sentence!

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.780
This is just the beginning.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:50.990
The version you know is sanitized for children's ears.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.200
Now that you're nine, we trust you as full citizens,

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.750
so I'm telling you our true
history and the village secret.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.790
However, there are some racy parts.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.880
Ｓｅｘｕａｌ  ｈａｒａｓｓｍｅｎｔ！

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.550
Please, continue.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.720
Don't blame me! It's an ancient tradition.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:14.640
Ｄｏｎ'ｔ  ｔｏｕｃｈ  ｍｅ！

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.890
I give up. Have your mom tell you later, Kaori.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:24.520
This might be rough for you guys,
but most folktales like this are pretty raw.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.030
In fact, this is fairly tame.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:31.240
Though it does feature one of life's great mysteries!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.780
What happens?!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:41.330
When the maiden faced the bear,
she trembled in terror at his great size.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:47.050
"If I am to be eaten, then at
least I shall neuter this beast."

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:50.630
The bear stalked toward her
with exquisite seductiveness...

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.430
and insinuated his tongue between her legs.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.600
"Oh, you loathsome bear!"

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:00.890
"The sensation of your tongue
against me has made me lose control!"

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:04.150
"Yes! No! You terrible beast!"

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.610
All their children had the bodies of bears.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.700
This is the beginning of the Kumai clan.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.740
See? Not too bad, right?

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.780
R-Right.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.410
There <i>are</i> lots of people named Kumai in our village.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.960
You were listening?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.170
The bear fell for the maiden, mended his ways,

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.130
and began working hard for the village.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.300
Kumade Village became jointly
governed by humans and Kumai.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.090
But hey, it's just a legend.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.930
Don't forget it, though, because...

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:42.140
the bears here can speak to humans!

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:51.360
I mean, of course. Otherwise we'd never get along!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.240
The connection between villagers and Kumai thrives to this day.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.780
Did he just say bears can talk?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:58.080
Your moms always say "Bears eat naughty kids," right?

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:58.080
I'm worried. He looked serious.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.490
They mean it!

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.490
Is he having a breakdown?

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:03.580
The civil service job must be too much for him.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.330
Oh, juice!

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.540
Thank you!

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.380
I was looking for... juice...

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:13.420
Natsu!

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:18.430
Yoshio! It's a b-b-bear! We gotta run!

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.810
"Graawrrr!"

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.140
Just kidding.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:29.560
It's fine! Bears in our village don't eat people.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.570
It's part of the deal.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:32.940
It's fine! Come on, pet him.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.160
I guess he's not in the mood!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.870
Anyway, it's Kumade Shrine
that executed the contract...

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:51.300
and mediates our coexistence with the Kumai.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:57.630
And its miko, the maiden with mystic powers who leads the ceremonies...

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.100
is Amayadori Machi!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.390
Again this year?

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.650
Is she even dressed up?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.900
Well, what can you do?

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.900
Bring her in for me, would you?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.660
No!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.580
I don't wanna go!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:29.620
Put me down, Natsu! I don't need to say hello!

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:35.800
So, this is the bear miko, and Kumai Natsu, the Kumai representative.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.840
Make sure you venerate them appropriately!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.590
It's Machi!

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.850
Oh, you're Yoshio's cousin!

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.970
Never knew you had such a distinguished job.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.980
It's not distinguished.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.850
I can't face them after that dirty story!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:55.360
I don't need to be here! You guys chat by yourselves!

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:59.200
Huh? They're really scared of you.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:04.200
The Women's Association told me to be more intimidating.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.080
Okay!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:10.790
Now let's have Machi favor us with a few words!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.650
I'm sorry for the harassment.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:38.150
And now some words from Natsu, since she didn't fill her time slot!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.700
I don't have anything prepared.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.280
Yoshio's just messing with us, as usual.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.910
Anything'll do.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.910
Anything?

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.330
Kumaan.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.290
Yoshio! What did the bear mean?

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.880
He said, "Kumaan"...

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:02.970
Ah, that one means "I like apples!"

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.430
It's just a sound he makes.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.600
You're such a joker, Natsu!

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.350
My favorite food is sushi.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:13.310
It's nice to meet you.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:16.820
Wow! He really does speak!

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:20.650
I thought the village was boring, but I can brag about this!

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.530
No, you can't.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:27.660
If you reveal the village secret, you'll be punished!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.370
Machi, you're so cool!

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.620
Hey, do you ever wear miko clothes?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.590
S-Sometimes.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.170
Every day...

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.960
Thanks for all your work.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.050
I'm sure it's tough, but you can do it!

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:45.930
Hey, Machi.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:47.600
What?

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.320
Did the bear do you, too?

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.400
"Do me"...

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.200
D-Do... me...

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:08.450
No!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:11.080
The miko and the sacrificial
virgin are different people—

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.000
Don't imagine it!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.660
Did he, Machi?

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.210
You two are so close, you...

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.210
You big dummy!

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:19.090
You're in middle school, and you've already done it?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.500
And with a bear...

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.090
I can't allow this!

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.220
Moron!

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.470
<i>Don't</i> imagine it!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.140
Dummy! Blockhead! Stupid!

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.310
That would never happen!

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:35.520
According to town records, the origin of the miko is—

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:36.480
Nothing happened.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.480
I've been neutered.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:48.490
How cruelly, indecently unfair...

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.490
village society is.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.490
Great, we can breathe easy!

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.490
Dummy!

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:56.500
And yet, we continue our lives, here in this village.

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:30.550
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:34.010
I'm hungry.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.600
Did you eat your snack?

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:38.850
Yeah.

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:42.600
I found some pickles.

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:47.360
Snacking on pickles and tea...

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.400
She's like an old lady.
